@meeting introHealth
// Day 2, Tuesday 14:00, the infirmary: Rina's new-crew health check (Writer 5, batch 9, for onboarding's hook).
// Needs, energy, the Needs app, bonuses and penalties, in her dry way. One choice, no wrong answer. Nothing about
// her exam.
title: Your health check
from: Rina Deshi
gist: Rina's health check: your needs are in the Needs app. High ones help, low ones slow you down. Drink some water.
== lines
rina: You're my two o'clock. Sit. Arm out. Don't touch anything blue.   [gesture]
rina > you: Needs. Hunger, energy, hygiene, social, fitness. They're on your device, in the Needs app.
rina: Keep one high and it helps. You work faster, or walk faster. That's the good news.
rina: Let one drop low and it slows you down. Nothing worse. You'll just feel it.
rina: Eat in the mess. Sleep in your bunk. Shower. Talk to people. The gym, if you must.
? choice
* What if I forget?   flavour:practical
  rina: Your device marks it. Up for good, down for bad. You'll learn.   [nod]
* Do you check yours?   flavour:share
  rina: Every hour. Mostly I just drink water.
* (Hold out your arm)
  rina: Good. You're a better patient than Pell already.   [laugh]
rina: Done. Drink some water on the way out. That's not a suggestion.
